{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"═══ CANONICAL HANDOFF — READ THIS FIRST, THEN TRUST THE STORE OVER ANY PROMPT ═══\n\n**CLOSED (11):** 7761, 172e, 343b, 7cbe, b00f, d8ef, b300, b5fe, d23e, epic 9227, eb58.\n**OPEN, claimed by me:** 3768 (in_progress), b690 (in_progress).\n**OPEN, blocked:** 0d76 (S6) <- eb6e (S8) <- 8625 (S9). **READY:** 5e75.\n**GERRIT:** 1164 (d23e) and 1169 (3768) both LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1 / submittable. **NOTHING SUBMITTED** — the stack lands only when epic 061c closes.\n\n**THE ONE THING THAT MATTERS RIGHT NOW: b690.** The code-review gate NEVER honours per-step model classes. Proven by a live run: nine calls, every one on `cfg.model`, INCLUDING `code-review-verify` whose `model: standard` was landed by 172e — so it is pre-existing, not a regression from 3768. b690 (story, parented to 061c, plan CERTIFIED) carries the fix. Its comments hold the full investigation: the measured design decision, five eliminated hypotheses, the test-design constraint, and a fully-determined 5-step implementation order. START THERE, not from scratch.\n\n**3768 is blocked BY b690, not broken.** Its YAML is correct and its change is green on Gerrit; its remaining [operator-attested] criterion asks for a live run showing per-pass model ids, and that run currently DISPROVES the behaviour. It closes after b690 lands.\n\n**HOW TO GET STATE (never trust a prompt's snapshot):** `rebar ready` for claimability (the `deps` field is NOT the blocker list); a plan review on a blocked ticket fast-fails with NO LLM spend and names the blockers for free; `rebar review-plan <id> --status` for attestation currency; Gerrit votes via `o=DETAILED_LABELS` reading `all[].value` (`o=LABELS` omits `value` and reports a false all-zeros).\n\n**LANDING CAUTION:** open changes under this identity include work from a CONCURRENT SESSION in /Users/joeoakhart/impl-42eb-tickets-clone (tickets 5200, e161). Submit ONLY changes whose `rebar-ticket:` trailer names one of THIS epic's tickets. A change can carry both +1s and still not be submittable — the no-unresolved-comments condition is real and invisible to a votes-only check.\n\n**STANDING DECISIONS (do not relitigate):** REBAR_LLM_MODEL uses `_scheduled` not `_permanent` (the parent decided it, and the six `_permanent` precedents are RENAMES, not supersessions). Deprecation emission is PER CALL — 'once per process' was withdrawn as unmechanised. The warning lives at every ENV READ and nowhere else, never in `resolve_model_string` where provenance is already lost. `resolve_verifier_model`'s equality rule is SUPERSEDED AND CALLERLESS — never cite it as a live defect. 9227's LOC criterion tracks the enforced <700 seam bound, not a hand-carried number. eb6e's kill-switch durability note is the operator's call — do not edit eb6e's plan. The per-FUNCTION length ratchet is REJECTED.\n\n**IN-SCOPE RULING FROM THE OPERATOR:** fixing the review plumbing to honour the 3-class configuration IS epic work; so is closing 172e's evidence gap. Tickets may be filed under the epic for in-scope work and outside it for unrelated work. **The epic's mandate is to ship WITHOUT BUGS — ASK before declaring any bug out of scope.**"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785616207227038001,"uuid":"a63229c4-2890-48d6-abee-d2b9c1af0082"}